7,"away_games":18,"home_all":113,"away_all":37},"basis":{"min_games":18,"team_news":true},"h2h":[{"date":"2024-02-03","home":"4057","away":"103","score":[2,3]},{"date":"2023-12-02","home":"103","away":"4057","score":[3,1]}],"analyst_view":{"overall":"Milan (5th, 24 points, four wins in five) host Frosinone (7th, 20 points), whose attack has been one of the league's busiest even though they lost 1-0 at Cagliari before the break. Frosinone under Alvini miss top scorer Raimondo (injured) and the suspended Bracaglia, both counted by the numbers; Birligea leads the line with Ghedjemis, Schmidt and Kvernadze behind him and Terzic at left-back. For Milan, Tomori is ruled out with a hamstring injury (not on the numbers' list, back for Cagliari) along with Gabbia, Loftus-Cheek, Chukwueze and Saelemaekers, and Pavlovic is still being judged day by day after his kidney problem, so the expected back four is Gila, De Winter, Diawara and Bartesaghi; Maignan is fit after his scare with France and Pulisic, back from the US only on Friday, is listed to start behind Gonçalo Ramos. Referee Luca Pairetto (4.9 cards a game) is already in the numbers; no official lineups were out when this was refreshed an hour before kick-off.","goals":{"lean":"higher","adjust_pct":3,"call":"Around 3.2 goals","text":"The numbers say 3.1 goals, already cut a lot for Raimondo's absence (-19% on Frosinone's goals) and raised a little for both sides' recent form. Tomori, not on the numbers' list, is out and Pavlovic is short of fitness, so Diawara is expected beside De Winter in a makeshift back line against a fast, direct Frosinone side; Pulisic, back late from the US, is still expected to start, so I keep the mild nudge to about 3.2."},"corners":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10 corners","text":"The numbers say 9.9 corners and already raise Frosinone's side for their big recent corner count (+9%) while trimming Milan's (-4%). Frosinone's wingers Ghedjemis and Kvernadze drive that count and Milan have won few corners lately, both already in the figure, and the match-day news changes nothing in the wide areas, so I stay at about 9.9."},"cards":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 5 cards","text":"The numbers say 5.1 cards and already add Pairetto's strict record (+35%; 4.9 a game over 31 games). It is not a rivalry and no new suspension risk was reported; Frosinone's quick wingers may draw fouls from a reshuffled Milan defence, but not enough to move a figure that already carries a strict referee, so I stay at about 5.1."},"shots":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 33 shots","text":"The numbers say 33.3 shots, already lifted heavily for Frosinone's shooting (+24%) and cut for Milan's low recent volume (-6%). Milan's expected attack around Ramos, Pulisic and Moreira is their usual one, and Birligea has been Frosinone's starter for weeks, so the shooting volume should look like recent games; about 33."},"shots_on_target":{"lean":"higher","adjust_pct":3,"call":"Around 11.1 on target","text":"The numbers say 10.8 shots on target, already raised for Frosinone's sharp recent form (+21%). With Tomori out (not counted) and Pavlovic not fully fit, Diawara is expected to start in a reshaped back line, which should give Frosinone's runners cleaner looks; a small nudge to about 11.1."},"sources":["https://www.pazzidifanta.com/news/milan-frosinone-probabili-formazioni-12a-giornata-serie-a-2026-2027-460771","https://www.pazzidifanta.com/news/milan-ultime-infermeria-cista-match-frosinone-460732","https://www.fantamaster.it/milan-frosinone-12-giornata-allarme-pulisic-gestione-fantacalcio/","https://www.fantacalcio.it/serie-a/calendario/12/2026-27/milan-frosinone/18070","https://www.sportsmole.co.uk/football/serie-a/ac-milan-vs-frosinone_game_263293.html","https://www.tuttomercatoweb.com/serie-a/milan-esame-frosinone-bologna-vede-europa-2295367"],"written_at":"2026-11-22T16:10:00Z"},"league":"serie-a","take":{"applied":true,"written_at":"2026-11-22T16:1